{:edb/db-before-t 609 :edb/db-after-t 610 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533922 50 #inst "2026-10-05T13:13:21.479Z" 13194139533922 true] [17592186083155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266131 13194139533922 true] [17592186083155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266138 13194139533922 true] [17592186083155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266142 13194139533922 true] [17592186083158 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266117 13194139533922 true] [17592186083158 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266124 13194139533922 true] [17592186266117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266118 13194139533922 true] [17592186266117 1089 "q-102941" 13194139533922 true] [17592186266117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533922 true] [17592186266117 1100 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\frac{4}{\\pi }{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" 13194139533922 true] [17592186266117 1113 #uuid "3bd401ff-d3f2-5dd6-97bc-c215e66b66ce" 13194139533922 true] [17592186266117 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{8}{\\pi }t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{\\pi }t)}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2})}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533922 true] [17592186266118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266119 13194139533922 true] [17592186266118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266120 13194139533922 true] [17592186266118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266121 13194139533922 true] [17592186266118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266122 13194139533922 true] [17592186266118 1000 #edb/ref 175